From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cbm <omarchy-mobile@kloot.lu>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:46:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: i2c: add onsemi LC898129

The LC898129 is a microcontroller that drives a camera module's focus
and optical image stabilisation actuators and holds the module's
calibration memory, over I2C with 16-bit register addresses and 32-bit
values. The Google Pixel 9a's main camera module has one. It shares the
module's supplies and reset with the image sensor, so the sensor powers
it while streaming through its lens-focus property. The supplies follow
the stock device tree's actuator node: the I/O supply, the actuator
driver's VM and its analogue VDDA. All are optional, since the sensor
already switches them; listed, they only keep the rails counted.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: cbm <omarchy-mobile@kloot.lu>
---
 .../bindings/media/i2c/onnn,lc898129.yaml     | 54 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/onnn,lc898129.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/onnn,lc898129.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/onnn,lc898129.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..d2f0d719a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/onnn,lc898129.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/media/i2c/onnn,lc898129.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: onsemi LC898129 camera lens autofocus and stabilisation controller
+
+maintainers:
+  - cbm <omarchy-mobile@kloot.lu>
+
+description:
+  The onsemi LC898129 is a microcontroller that drives a camera module's
+  focus and optical image stabilisation actuators and holds the module's
+  calibration memory, controlled over I2C with 16-bit register addresses
+  and 32-bit values. It shares the module's supplies and reset with the
+  image sensor, which powers it while streaming (the sensor's lens-focus
+  property). It is the controller of the Google Pixel 9a's main camera
+  module.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: onnn,lc898129
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  vio-supply:
+    description: Interface (1.8 V) supply.
+
+  vm-supply:
+    description: Actuator driver supply (VM).
+
+  vdda-supply:
+    description: Actuator driver analogue supply (VDDA).
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        lens@24 {
+            compatible = "onnn,lc898129";
+            reg = <0x24>;
+            vio-supply = <&vddio_cam>;
+        };
+    };
